    <body>
        <header>
            <h1>Generative AI Competitive Landscape</h1>
            <div class="subtitle">User Sentiment & Complaint Analysis Across Top 5 AI Apps (Q1 2026)</div>
        </header>

        <div class="container">
            <!-- Executive Overview -->
            <section id="executive-overview">
                <h2>Executive Overview</h2>
                <p>This report analyzes 50,000 user reviews across the top five generative AI mobile applications: ChatGPT, Microsoft Copilot, Google Gemini, Perplexity, and Claude. By examining star ratings, sentiment polarity, and thematic complaints, we derived actionable intelligence on competitive positioning and user friction points.</p>
                <div class="takeaways">
                    <h3>Top 3 Strategic Takeaways</h3>
                    <ol>
                        <li><strong>Accuracy Overcomes Interface:</strong> Apps perceived as having higher accuracy generally maintain better sentiment scores, even if they have bug-related complaints.</li>
                        <li><strong>The Paywall Penalty:</strong> Pricing and subscription complaints are major drivers of negative sentiment and low star ratings, signaling a highly price-sensitive user base.</li>
                        <li><strong>Sentiment Divergence Reveals Hidden Frustration:</strong> A notable percentage of 4- and 5-star reviews exhibit negative text sentiment, indicating sarcasm or users who are conceptually impressed but practically frustrated.</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- Cross-App Sentiment Comparison -->
            <section id="app-sentiment-comparison">
                <h2>Cross-App Sentiment Comparison</h2>
                <div class="grid-2">
                    <div class="chart-container">
